class Solution {
public:
    int maxWaterBottles(int numBottles, int numExchange) {
        int totalBottles = numBottles;  // Initialize the total bottles consumed
        int emptyBottles = numBottles;  // Initialize the empty bottles available for exchange

        while (emptyBottles >= numExchange) {
            int newBottles = emptyBottles / numExchange;  // Calculate the new bottles obtained from exchanging empty ones
            totalBottles += newBottles;  // Add the new bottles to the total consumed
            emptyBottles = newBottles + (emptyBottles % numExchange);  // Update the empty bottles after exchange
        }

        return totalBottles;
    }
};
```

The `maxWaterBottles` function iteratively calculates the total number of water bottles consumed by exchanging empty bottles for full ones based on the given exchange rate. It keeps track of the total bottles consumed and the remaining empty bottles after each exchange until no more exchanges are possible. Finally, it returns the total number of water bottles consumed.

