int maxNonAdjacentSum(int a[], int n) {
    if (n <= 0) return 0;

    int incl = a[0];  // Maximum sum including the previous element
    int excl = 0;      // Maximum sum excluding the previous element

    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        // Current maximum excluding i
        int newExcl = (incl > excl) ? incl : excl;

        // Current maximum including i
        incl = excl + a[i];

        // Update excl for next iteration
        excl = newExcl;
    }

    // Return the maximum of incl and excl
    return (incl > excl) ? incl : excl;
}
```

The function `maxNonAdjacentSum` iterates through the array, maintaining the maximum sum including and excluding the current element. It then returns the maximum of the two sums as the result. This approach ensures that no two adjacent elements are included in the subarray sum.

