In the solution, we use a queue to keep track of the nodes to be visited. We start with the given startNode, mark it as visited, and add it to the queue. Then, we iterate through the queue, visiting each node and adding its adjacent nodes to the queue if they have not been visited before. Finally, we return the result vector containing the order of visited nodes during the BFS traversal.

