double averageEdgeLength(const Surface_mesh& mesh, const Surface_mesh::Vertex_property<Vec3>& points) {
    double totalLength = 0.0;
    int edgeCount = 0;

    for (auto eit = mesh.edges_begin(); eit != mesh.edges_end(); ++eit) {
        auto h = mesh.halfedge(*eit, 0);
        auto v0 = mesh.to_vertex(h);
        auto v1 = mesh.from_vertex(h);
        Vec3 p0 = points[v0];
        Vec3 p1 = points[v1];
        double edgeLength = (p1 - p0).norm();
        totalLength += edgeLength;
        edgeCount++;
    }

    if (edgeCount > 0) {
        return totalLength / edgeCount;
    } else {
        return 0.0;  // Return 0 if there are no edges in the mesh
    }
}
```

In the solution, we iterate through all the edges of the mesh, calculate the length of each edge using the vertex positions, and accumulate the total length and count of edges. Finally, we return the average edge length by dividing the total length by the number of edges. If the mesh has no edges, we return 0.0 as the average edge length.

