bool searchMatrix(int matrix[][4], int rows, int cols, int target) {
    if (rows == 0 || cols == 0) {
        return false;
    }

    int row = 0;
    int col = cols - 1;

    while (row < rows && col >= 0) {
        if (matrix[row][col] == target) {
            return true;
        } else if (matrix[row][col] > target) {
            col--;
        } else {
            row++;
        }
    }

    return false;
}
```

The `searchMatrix` function starts from the top-right corner of the matrix. It compares the value at this position with the target value. If the value is equal to the target, it returns true. If the value is greater than the target, it moves left in the same row. If the value is less than the target, it moves down to the next row. This process continues until the target is found or the search goes out of bounds, in which case it returns false.

