You are tasked with implementing a custom smart pointer class similar to `boost::shared_ptr` using C++ templates. The custom smart pointer should provide reference counting and automatic memory management features.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `CustomSharedPtr` class, which should have the following features:
1. It should be a template class that can hold any type of object.
2. It should manage the reference count of the object it points to.
3. It should automatically release the memory when the reference count becomes zero.
4. It should support the dereferencing operator (`*`) and the member access operator (`->`).

You need to implement the following member functions for the `CustomSharedPtr` class:
1. A constructor that takes a pointer to an object and initializes the reference count.
2. A copy constructor that increments the reference count.
3. A destructor that decrements the reference count and releases the memory if the reference count becomes zero.
4. An overloaded assignment operator (`=`) that decrements the reference count of the old object and increments the reference count of the new object.
5. An overloaded dereferencing operator (`*`) that returns a reference to the object.
6. An overloaded member access operator (`->`) that returns a pointer to the object.

You should use the given code snippet as a starting point and complete the implementation of the `CustomSharedPtr` class.

```cpp
template <typename T>
class CustomSharedPtr
{
public:
    // Constructor
    CustomSharedPtr(T* ptr) : m_ptr(ptr), m_refCount(new int(1)) {}

    // Copy constructor
    CustomSharedPtr(const CustomSharedPtr<T>& other) : m_ptr(other.m_ptr), m_refCount(other.m_refCount)
    {
        (*m_refCount)++;
    }

    // Destructor
    ~CustomSharedPtr()
    {
        (*m_refCount)--;
        if (*m_refCount == 0)
        {
            delete m_ptr;
            delete m_refCount;
        }
    }

    // Assignment operator
    CustomSharedPtr<T>& operator=(const CustomSharedPtr<T>& other)
    {
        if (this != &other)
        {
            (*m_refCount)--;
            if (*m_refCount == 0)
            {
                delete m_ptr;
                delete m_refCount;
            }
            m_ptr = other.m_ptr;
            m_refCount = other.m_refCount;
            (*m_refCount)++;
        }
        return *this;
    }

    // Dereferencing operator
    T& operator*() const
    {
        return *m_ptr;
    }

    // Member access operator
    T* operator->() const
    {
        return m_ptr;
    }

private:
    T* m_ptr;
    int* m_refCount;
};
```

