    if (root->left == nullptr && root->right == nullptr) {
        return sum == root->val;
    }
    return hasPathSum(root->left, sum - root->val) || hasPathSum(root->right, sum - root->val);
}
```
The solution uses a recursive approach to traverse the tree. If the current node is a leaf and the remaining sum is equal to the value of the leaf node, it returns true. Otherwise, it recursively checks the left and right subtrees with the updated sum. If any of the recursive calls return true, the function returns true, indicating the existence of a path with the given sum. If no such path is found, the function returns false.

