#include <string>

class StringManipulator {
public:
    std::string reverseString(std::string s) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = s.length() - 1;
        while (left < right) {
            std::swap(s[left], s[right]);
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return s;
    }
};
```

The `reverseString` function uses a two-pointer approach to reverse the input string `s`. It initializes two pointers, `left` at the beginning of the string and `right` at the end of the string. It then iteratively swaps the characters at the `left` and `right` positions, moving towards the center of the string until the pointers meet. Finally, the reversed string is returned.

